# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#

# --- AirTrail's dedicated Postgres database ---
# AirTrail (a flight-logging app) ships its own Postgres container in this
# stack rather than using the shared central `postgres` stack. These three
# values are used TWICE in docker-compose.yml: once to configure AirTrail's
# postgres container itself (POSTGRES_USER/POSTGRES_PASSWORD/POSTGRES_DB),
# and again to build AirTrail's own DB_URL connection string
# (postgres://...@postgres:5432/...) that the airtrail app container uses
# to reach it. Keep all three in sync -- they describe the same database
# from both sides.
#
# This is still a plain-text credential in .env for now -- this stack
# hasn't been migrated to file-based Docker secrets (the way the central
# postgres/Authentik/Infisical stacks have).
#
# Note: this stack's docker-compose.yml has no traefik.* labels at all,
# even though the airtrail service sets ORIGIN to an external.valdeze.ch
# hostname and joins shared-services with a Docker network alias -- so it's
# not clear from this repo alone whether it's routed via Traefik's
# separate file-based (dynamic/) config, or not Traefik-routed yet at all.
# Worth confirming rather than assuming it's reachable today.
DB_USERNAME=REPLACE_ME
DB_DATABASE_NAME=REPLACE_ME
DB_PASSWORD=REPLACE_ME
